    comment: 'the 288 samples that start the frame, in the units of the stock IFFT (8 x the model): the STS (128 samples: a 64-sample IFFT of 6 QPSK subcarriers k = +-4, +-8, +-12 sent twice, so the signal repeats every 16 samples) and the LTS (a prefix of 32 samples, the training symbol of 28 QPSK subcarriers, the same symbol again: 160 samples). They are not OFDM symbols with the usual 16-sample prefix, so the carrier allocator does not make them'
